// ── C1 (plan 02 §11): the planets' two-tier mean motion OF DATE,
// mirroring Earth's shipped sidereal-year channel exactly:
//   n_p(y) = λ̇₀_p · lamDotRel_p(y) / massLossRatio(y)
// λ̇₀_p = the banked channel's secular J2000 rate (2-kyr boxcar — the
// window is named in the hovers; it averages the great-inequality /
// U–N wiggles that the era-window winN partially absorbs into its fit,
// and matches JPL-class periods — the measured decomposition split is
// banked in verdict.planetLamDot, Neptune −497 ppm the largest).
// lamDotRel_p = the planet's own constant-GM N-body drift (±10 Myr,
// CLAMPED beyond — refuse-to-extrapolate). massLossRatio = the ONE
// Driver-2 law shared by every heliocentric orbit (planet-independence
